      "math_academy_id": "e-10840",
      "problem": "Compute $P\\left( X > 8 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14122876/assets/93b9c1704c44df8e09662fd79503c3f01477230157d6f436c0c0bf937579da69.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a <    X <    b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }5{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-5x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14122876/observations/step-e10840-fcab56c63cadbf04b173.html",
